        "id": 9627,
        "name": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-21T22:09:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>As a few of you might know, I've been pseudo-unemployed since June of last year, when my previous school declined to give me a long-term contract.</p><p>Since then, I've been hunting for jobs, in addition to running my currently--totally unprofitable, as I have yet to have my flagship product released by my publisher--RPG company. &nbsp;</p><p>In January, I was hired by Kaplan as an SAT/ACT prep coach, but only on a part-time basis. &nbsp;My first (and only class) with them was cancelled, leaving me high and dry for both hours and pay. &nbsp;In fairly dire straights, I applied at a local Donato's Pizza as a delivery driver and was hired. &nbsp;I started there this week.</p><p>However, today, I was tendered an offer by another local school district as a long-term substitute teacher. &nbsp;I accepted the offer and would start on March 2nd.</p><p>The issue comes in what I do next. &nbsp;Between my few Kaplan hours and my subbing, we'll be fine financially through the rest of the school year. &nbsp;However, come June, I'll lose my primary method of employment, even if the district picks me up for the vacancy I'm subbing for (the prior teacher is retiring, so there's definitely a vacancy, for which I'll have the inside track). &nbsp;There's no way that I could potentially keep all three jobs, as Donato's has me primarily closing (which means being at the store until 1am most nights, making it unsuitable when I have to wake up at 6am to go teach). &nbsp;However, if I drop the Donato's job, I may be high and dry come June.</p><p>Thoughts? &nbsp;Ideas? &nbsp;Advice? &nbsp;I'll be working at Donato's tomorrow, so I will talk to them then, but what do I even say in this situation?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:40:27.787Z",
